WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.340 --> 00:00:02.915
On average, Americans spend 87%

00:00:02.915 --> 00:00:04.600
of their time indoors.

00:00:04.600 --> 00:00:06.590
But what if you ditched that last bit

00:00:06.590 --> 00:00:09.320
and gave up the great outdoors for good?

00:00:09.320 --> 00:00:11.630
Odds are you've been stuck at home before,

00:00:11.630 --> 00:00:13.530
maybe because of bad weather.

00:00:13.530 --> 00:00:16.380
Maybe there's a pandemic and
you're self-quarantining.

00:00:16.380 --> 00:00:18.840
You probably wouldn't notice
a huge difference at first,

00:00:18.840 --> 00:00:21.310
other than a bit of cabin fever.

00:00:21.310 --> 00:00:25.460
But after a week and a half,
things may start to change.

00:00:25.460 --> 00:00:27.960
Ironically, after spending
all that time indoors,

00:00:27.960 --> 00:00:29.810
you may start to feel tired,

00:00:29.810 --> 00:00:31.840
no matter how much sleep you get.

00:00:31.840 --> 00:00:33.877
You see, being stuck inside

00:00:33.877 --> 00:00:36.120
limits the amount of sunlight you get.

00:00:36.120 --> 00:00:37.860
Normally, when sunlight hits your eyes,

00:00:37.860 --> 00:00:39.960
it signals to your brain to stop producing

00:00:39.960 --> 00:00:42.320
a hormone called melatonin,

00:00:42.320 --> 00:00:44.600
and that hormone affects
your circadian rhythm,

00:00:44.600 --> 00:00:46.380
which regulates sleep.

00:00:46.380 --> 00:00:48.370
Without a reliable sunlight trigger,

00:00:48.370 --> 00:00:50.850
your body will just keep making melatonin,

00:00:50.850 --> 00:00:54.700
and it might start to
feel tired all the time.

00:00:54.700 --> 00:00:56.790
Sunlight is also a trigger for your body

00:00:56.790 --> 00:01:00.770
to produce serotonin,
aka the happy hormone.

00:01:00.770 --> 00:01:03.320
It helps to regulate your
mood, among other things.

00:01:03.320 --> 00:01:06.010
So without enough sunlight,
after a few months,

00:01:06.010 --> 00:01:07.920
your melatonin levels will rise,

00:01:07.920 --> 00:01:09.430
and your serotonin levels?

00:01:09.430 --> 00:01:12.200
Those may drop, along with your mood.

00:01:12.200 --> 00:01:15.430
It's this combination of
decreased sunlight and serotonin

00:01:15.430 --> 00:01:17.430
that's credited as one of the main causes

00:01:17.430 --> 00:01:20.670
of seasonal affective disorder, or SAD.

00:01:20.670 --> 00:01:22.740
It's a type of depression
that is most prevalent

00:01:22.740 --> 00:01:24.680
during long, dark months.

00:01:24.680 --> 00:01:26.810
SAD is relatively uncommon,

00:01:26.810 --> 00:01:30.940
but it may increase if we
all stay locked in our homes.

00:01:30.940 --> 00:01:32.330
You may be thinking you can just

00:01:32.330 --> 00:01:35.520
bring in artificial
sunlight, like a light box.

00:01:35.520 --> 00:01:39.040
Well, this has been shown to
reduce the effects of SAD,

00:01:39.040 --> 00:01:40.810
but not cure it.

00:01:40.810 --> 00:01:42.100
And it wouldn't really matter,

00:01:42.100 --> 00:01:43.500
because your mood can be affected

00:01:43.500 --> 00:01:45.500
by another important factor.

00:01:45.500 --> 00:01:47.240
The great outdoors.

00:01:47.240 --> 00:01:49.350
Just being outside in
general has been linked

00:01:49.350 --> 00:01:51.040
to lower stress levels.

00:01:51.040 --> 00:01:53.120
So say goodbye to staying calm,

00:01:53.120 --> 00:01:55.530
and hello to higher blood pressure.

00:01:55.530 --> 00:01:57.930
Plus, that inside air is stale.

00:01:57.930 --> 00:01:59.960
The Environmental Protection Agency says

00:01:59.960 --> 00:02:03.290
it's up to five times more
polluted than the air outdoors.

00:02:03.290 --> 00:02:05.610
This isn't good news for your lungs.

00:02:05.610 --> 00:02:08.200
Over time, breathing in that recycled air

00:02:08.200 --> 00:02:11.340
could increase your risk for
illnesses linked to pollution.

00:02:11.340 --> 00:02:13.600
And four months to a year down the road,

00:02:13.600 --> 00:02:15.843
your body is going to
start missing something

00:02:15.843 --> 00:02:18.620
vital to your health: vitamin D.

00:02:18.620 --> 00:02:20.870
This is essential for optimal health,

00:02:20.870 --> 00:02:23.810
bone strength, and muscular regulation.

00:02:23.810 --> 00:02:25.724
In order to make vitamin D active,

00:02:25.724 --> 00:02:28.750
you need sunlight, and
artificial won't do.

00:02:28.750 --> 00:02:31.930
When ultraviolet B rays hit
cholesterol in your skin,

00:02:31.930 --> 00:02:33.900
energy is released, and that fuels

00:02:33.900 --> 00:02:35.670
the production of vitamin D.

00:02:35.670 --> 00:02:37.180
Without that production, though,

00:02:37.180 --> 00:02:39.450
your vitamin D levels will start to drop.

00:02:39.450 --> 00:02:42.040
And if you don't do anything
to counter this decrease,

00:02:42.040 --> 00:02:43.930
you might find yourself losing strength

00:02:43.930 --> 00:02:45.440
or getting depressed,

00:02:45.440 --> 00:02:48.350
while your bones gradually become weaker.

00:02:48.350 --> 00:02:50.240
Vitamin D is also important

00:02:50.240 --> 00:02:52.210
for regulating your immune system,

00:02:52.210 --> 00:02:56.120
so you could be at a higher
risk of catching illnesses, too.

00:02:56.120 --> 00:02:58.920
The next development is
a little hard to predict,

00:02:58.920 --> 00:03:02.290
since vitamin D levels
vary from person to person.

00:03:02.290 --> 00:03:05.030
But you may start seeing
some very serious issues

00:03:05.030 --> 00:03:06.620
in a few years.

00:03:06.620 --> 00:03:09.170
Lower levels of vitamin D
could put you at a higher risk

00:03:09.170 --> 00:03:11.610
of developing heart disease or strokes,

00:03:11.610 --> 00:03:14.760
plus an increased risk of
cancers, fractured bones,

00:03:14.760 --> 00:03:17.090
and serious tooth decay.

00:03:17.090 --> 00:03:19.370
Years down the road, you
might feel some pains,

00:03:19.370 --> 00:03:21.270
specifically in your bones and hips.

00:03:21.270 --> 00:03:23.040
You could even have difficulty walking,

00:03:23.040 --> 00:03:26.370
finding yourself waddling
or swaying precariously.

00:03:26.370 --> 00:03:28.480
Now, vitamin D supplements may or may not

00:03:28.480 --> 00:03:31.360
help replenish that loss
of activated vitamin D.

00:03:31.360 --> 00:03:33.960
But even with that
help, you might struggle

00:03:33.960 --> 00:03:35.940
from a lack of mental stimulation.

00:03:35.940 --> 00:03:38.380
In other words, you'll be bored.

00:03:38.380 --> 00:03:40.950
The monotony of everyday
life in the same place

00:03:40.950 --> 00:03:43.140
doing the same things over and over again,

00:03:43.140 --> 00:03:45.090
without stepping outdoors...

00:03:45.090 --> 00:03:47.740
that may all start to take a toll.

00:03:47.740 --> 00:03:49.270
If you don't have to go outside,

00:03:49.270 --> 00:03:51.510
you're likely to become more sedentary,

00:03:51.510 --> 00:03:53.665
meaning you'll exercise less.

00:03:53.665 --> 00:03:56.360
And research has shown that
even a short 12-minute walk

00:03:56.360 --> 00:03:58.270
can reduce symptoms of depression

00:03:58.270 --> 00:04:00.260
and help you cope with stress.

00:04:00.260 --> 00:04:02.980
This could be worse if
you live by yourself.

00:04:02.980 --> 00:04:05.360
Social isolation and
loneliness have been linked

00:04:05.360 --> 00:04:07.180
to conditions like high blood pressure,

00:04:07.180 --> 00:04:09.770
heart disease, anxiety, and depression.

00:04:09.770 --> 00:04:12.146
And if you're quarantined,
you could be dealing with

00:04:12.146 --> 00:04:14.396
a range of psychological stressors,

00:04:14.396 --> 00:04:16.550
resulting in undesirable symptoms

00:04:16.550 --> 00:04:18.580
like low mood and irritability,

00:04:18.580 --> 00:04:20.960
along with insomnia and depression,

00:04:20.960 --> 00:04:23.400
all made worse by the
fact that you'll be inside

00:04:23.400 --> 00:04:26.170
day after day doing the same thing.

00:04:26.170 --> 00:04:29.850
So maybe, if you can, go
and take a walk outside.

00:04:29.850 --> 00:04:32.780
And if you can't, well,
try staying active.

00:04:32.780 --> 00:04:35.150
Open a window to let fresh air in.

00:04:35.150 --> 00:04:37.430
Find ways to bring more
sunlight into your home

00:04:37.430 --> 00:04:39.910
so you don't mess up your sleep schedule.

00:04:39.910 --> 00:04:42.100
It also wouldn't hurt
to form a support system

00:04:42.100 --> 00:04:44.450
to keep you connected
with the outside world.

00:04:44.450 --> 00:04:47.460
Set up video chats or call
your family and friends.

00:04:47.460 --> 00:04:50.040
Others might be going
through a similar experience,

00:04:50.040 --> 00:04:52.730
and bonding over it could be validating,

00:04:52.730 --> 00:04:55.713
giving you what you need to get through.

